course: dictionary
lesson: 5275
title: Judge: a word with two jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A judge is a person, a noun. A judge is in charge of a court of law. Judges make sure trials are fair and decide punishments. «Adoption is made official by a judge in a family court.» Here judge names the person who does the important job.
explain: Judge can also be a doing word, a verb. To judge is to form an opinion, to decide who wins, or to estimate. «All these rules have one thing in common: they judge the person, not the act.» Here judge means form an opinion about someone.
explain: Use the words around judge to decide which meaning fits. A court, a trial or a prize means deciding. Distance, speed or size means estimating. «You judge distance by how many locations an army marches through» means you estimate how far it is.
fact: A judge is a person in charge of a court of law, and a judge must be fair.
fact: «Judge» can be a noun (a person) or a verb (a doing word): judge, judges, judged, judging.
fact: To judge a competition means to decide the winner.
fact: To judge a distance, size or speed means to estimate it.
fact: «Don't judge a book by its cover» means don't judge people by how they look.
exercise: «Adoption is made official by a judge in a family court.» What is a judge in this sentence? | To form an opinion about someone | *A person in charge of a court of law | A person who decides who wins a race | A cover for a book
exercise: «Don't judge a book by its cover.» What does judge mean here? | Estimate the size of the book | Decide who wins a book prize | *Form an opinion about someone or something | Read the book quickly
exercise: Before crossing the road, Ben must judge how fast the car is going. What does judge mean? | Count the number of cars | Decide who wins the race | *Estimate the speed | Stop and wait for ever
test: «The judges chose the best cake at the fair.» What do the judges do? | Estimate how far away the cake was | Work in a court of law | *Decide who wins the competition | Bake the cakes themselves
test: In maths, Maya must judge whether her answer is reasonable. What does judge mean? | Punish her for a wrong answer | Decide the winner of the maths quiz | *Estimate whether the answer is about right | Write the answer down slowly
exam: Which sentence uses judge as a verb (a doing word)? | *«All these rules judge the person, not the act.» | «Adoption is made official by a judge in a family court.» | «The judge ordered a fair trial.» | «She is a good judge of character.»
